# Copy to .env.local for local work. Never commit real values.

# Supabase project for the College Club (Project Settings > API)
SUPABASE_URL=https://hgjcnuwxhemynnvsnmou.supabase.co
# Secret server key. Keep it out of chat, email and the browser. Only set it in Vercel or .env.local.
SUPABASE_SERVICE_ROLE_KEY=

# The board's shared password for the dashboard's Financials page (at least 8 characters). Only in Vercel or .env.local,
# never in chat or the code. Typing it unlocks that browser for 30 days; changing it locks every browser at once.
# With none set, Financials is locked for everyone.
# DASHBOARD_FINANCIALS_PASSWORD=

# Leave unset in production. With no Supabase values, local development shows made-up sample data.
# CCS_ALLOW_SAMPLE_DATA=1

# Mailchimp (read-only reports). Put the API key only in Vercel or .env.local, never in chat.
# MAILCHIMP_API_KEY=
# MAILCHIMP_LIST_ID=f5e1cad862
# MAILCHIMP_SINCE=2022-01-01

# --- Member / reservation system (test build; see CLAUDE.md) ---
# The member area at /club shows only invented households. It exists while developing, or when
# CCS_ALLOW_SAMPLE_DATA=1 (set that in Vercel PREVIEW only), and never on the live production site.
# The member system's database. LOCAL or throwaway databases only (Supabase CLI: `supabase start`); the app refuses
# any address that looks like a hosted Supabase project. With this set, /club reads and writes Postgres instead of the
# in-memory sample. With CCS_ALLOW_SAMPLE_DATA=1 as well, the invented sample club is loaded the first time, if (and only
# if) the database has no households yet. Apply supabase/migrations first (`supabase db reset` does).
# CLUB_DATABASE_URL=postgresql://postgres:postgres@127.0.0.1:54322/postgres
# PREVIEWS ONLY: let a brand new, empty throwaway database set itself up from supabase/migrations on the first request (once,
# in order, remembering which files it has applied), and load the invented sample club. Without a shared database a Vercel
# preview keeps a separate private copy of the records in every server, so a saved booking or snack often does not show on the
# next page (CLAUDE.md, question CV). Needs CLUB_DATABASE_URL and CCS_ALLOW_SAMPLE_DATA=1 as well. Refused on the live site,
# wherever invented data is not allowed, and for any hosted Supabase address. The first request can take a minute or two.
# CLUB_AUTO_MIGRATE=1
# Used only by the automated tests (database rules, the Postgres store, and the browser tests against Postgres). Points at a
# local or throwaway Postgres; tests refuse Supabase addresses.
# CLUB_TEST_DATABASE_URL=postgresql://postgres:postgres@127.0.0.1:54322/postgres
# Freezes "now" for the member area (development and tests only), e.g. 2026-10-28T20:00:00Z. Leave unset otherwise.
# CCS_CLUB_NOW=
# The secret behind personal RSVP links in emails (step 4). At least 16 random characters; keep it out of chat, email and the
# browser. Set it wherever links must work (for example Vercel PREVIEW). While developing on your own computer a random one is
# made for each run; a deployed build with none has no links at all, rather than a different secret on every server.
# CLUB_LINK_SECRET=
# The secret behind the front-desk iPad's private address (member check-in). At least 16 random characters; keep it out of chat,
# email and the browser. Anyone with the address can use the iPad screens (check in, nothing else); changing this value switches
# the old address off at once. Staff see the current address on the Staff office > Front-desk iPad page. Set it wherever the
# iPad must work (for example Vercel PREVIEW). While developing on your own computer a random one is made for each run; a
# deployed build with none has no iPad at all, rather than a different address on every server.
# CLUB_IPAD_SECRET=
# Who counts as club staff when signing in (step 6). Entries separated by semicolons or new lines, each one an email address, an
# equals sign and the name the record should show, for example:
#   CLUB_STAFF_LOGINS="alex.staffer@example.org=Alex Staffer; sam.deskwell@example.org=Sam Deskwell"
# This holds real people's addresses, so it lives only in private settings (Vercel or .env.local), never in the code. A mistake
# in it is refused in words. Where the member area is switched off the list is ignored.
# CLUB_STAFF_LOGINS=
# The public address of this site, used in sign-in emails so a link always points here. Required wherever real email is sent;
# in a test build (where the "email" only appears on the test outbox page) the address of the request itself is used.
# CLUB_SITE_URL=https://example.org
# Where every "Member login" link on the public pages goes. Leave unset to use this site's own sign-in page (/club/sign-in). To give
# members a separate address (for example https://members.collegeclubseattle.com), set it here and redeploy: the pages pick it up
# everywhere at once. It must start with https:// (http://localhost is allowed for development); anything else is ignored and the
# default is used. This is only the link: pointing that address at this app is a Vercel and domain change, made by whoever holds
# the domain. The address is part of the built site, so a change needs a new deploy.
# NEXT_PUBLIC_MEMBER_APP_URL=
# Who is emailed when someone fills in the public Request a tour form. Leave unset to use the public membership address
# (membership@collegeclubseattle.com). A real email is only sent once the real email sender is switched on (see RESEND_API_KEY);
# either way every request is saved and shown on the staff office's Tour requests screen.
# CLUB_TOUR_NOTIFY_TO=
# The real email sender (Resend). All of these are private settings: the key goes only in Vercel or .env.local, never in chat or
# the code. Real email is used only where the member area is switched on for real members; anywhere invented data is allowed
# (development, previews, tests) sign-in "emails" go to the test outbox instead, even with these set, so a test build can never
# email anyone. A key with no CLUB_MAIL_FROM, or a wrong value, is refused in words and email sign-in then stays off.
# RESEND_API_KEY=
# What appears in the From line: an address on the domain verified in Resend, alone or with a name,
# for example College Club Seattle <no-reply@example.org>
# CLUB_MAIL_FROM=
# Where a member's reply goes. Leave unset to use the club's public membership address (membership@collegeclubseattle.com),
# set another address to change it, or set the word none to switch replies off.
# CLUB_MAIL_REPLY_TO=
# To prove the sender works before any member signs in, put the three settings above in .env.local and run:
#   npm run mail:test -- you@example.org
# It sends exactly one test email through the same sender code.
